# Runtime dependencies of the MCP tool-surface image (component `mcp`, MCP component).
#
# Four lines, and each earns its place by being imported at boot:
#   mcp        - the official Python SDK, `mcp.server.fastmcp` + `mcp.types`, the two names
#                local_observe/platform/mcp.py imports and refuses loudly without (the [project]
#                optional extra `mcp` in pyproject.toml pins the same version, and this line may not
#                drift from it: a surface built against another SDK is a different protocol version
#                than the one components/control/mcp/CONTRACT.md describes).
#   uvicorn    - the ASGI server the CMD line runs, exactly as components/control/platform does.
#   PyYAML     - local_observe/inventory/validation.py imports `yaml`, and tools.py imports
#                `canonical`/`timestamp` from that module, so the read surface cannot start without it.
#   jsonschema - the same module's `Draft202012Validator`.
#
# Transitive closure + sha256 hashes live in requirements.lock; regenerate as described in
# docs/BUILD.md. The platform's own lock (components/control/platform/requirements.lock) is the
# sibling; the two share the three base pins and must be regenerated together when one moves.
mcp==1.29.1
PyYAML==6.0.3
jsonschema==4.26.0
uvicorn==0.52.4
